//? Title: TFRecord I/O: Frames, Checksums and Feature Schemas
//? Subtitle: An empty record is data; end-of-file is the absence of another frame
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A stream of binary training examples needs exact boundaries, corruption detection and a known
feature schema. We round-trip empty and binary payloads through TFRecord compression modes,
then inspect typed tf.Example features and defaults. The native codec implements these formats
without a TensorFlow runtime; the examples measure storage rather than model accuracy.
)
\toc

> The method

Each uncompressed TFRecord frame consists of an eight-byte little-endian length, its four-byte
masked CRC-32C, the payload and its four-byte masked CRC-32C. For payload lengths L1..Ln,

$$
\mathrm{plain\ bytes}=\sum_i(L_i+16),\qquad
\mathrm{mask}(c)=\mathrm{rotateRight}(c,15)+\mathtt{0xa282ead8}\pmod{2^{32}}.
$$
\alttext(Every record adds sixteen bytes of framing, and each CRC is rotated and offset modulo two to the power thirty-two.)

CRC-32C uses the Castagnoli polynomial and differs from ZIP's CRC-32. It detects accidental
corruption, not deliberate tampering. GZIP or ZLIB wraps the complete framed stream; compression
must be supplied explicitly. An empty payload still has a complete frame. The current reader
materialises the file and records in memory rather than streaming lazily.
A tf.Example maps names to byte-string, Float32 or Int64 lists. ParseSingleExample returns features
in schema order, rejects present values with a wrong type/count and uses a supplied default for
an absent key. Use defaults matching the declared type/count. This minimal protobuf codec skips
supported unknown fields; it is not a general protobuf implementation. Work is linear in encoded size.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/tfrecord_io_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/tfrecord_io_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/tfrecord_io_concept.tikz > build/tfrecord_io_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/tfrecord_io_concept.svg build/tfrecord_io_concept.dvi > build/tfrecord_io_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/tfrecord_io_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
