> Simple examples

The payloads empty, a-NUL-b and last have lengths 0,3,4, so the plain file has 55 bytes. All three records must survive each compression mode in order.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tfrecord_io_sizes.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace d=dm::nn::data;
 const std::vector<std::string> records{"",std::string("a\0b",3),"last"};
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 dm::dstruct::DataFrame t;std::vector<std::string> mode;std::vector<double> sizes,count;
 for(const std::string compression:{"","GZIP","ZLIB"}){
 const auto path="build/tfrecord_"+(compression.empty()?std::string("plain"):compression);
 d::WriteTFRecords(path,records,compression);const auto read=d::ReadTFRecords(path,compression);
 if(read!=records)return 1;mode.push_back(compression.empty()?"plain":compression);sizes.push_back(std::filesystem::file_size(path));count.push_back(read.size());}
 if(sizes[0]!=55)return 1;
 t.add_column("compression",mode);t.add_column("file_bytes",sizes);t.add_column("records",count);
 auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.bars({0,1,2},sizes,"file bytes",{37,99,235},.5)
 .title("Tiny streams can grow under compression").x_label("plain=0, GZIP=1, ZLIB=2").y_label("bytes");
 p.size(820,420).save_svg("build/tfrecord_io_sizes.svg");std::print("{}\n",t.to_md());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| compression | file_bytes | records |
| :--- | ---: | ---: |
| plain | 55 | 3 |
| GZIP | 60 | 3 |
| ZLIB | 48 | 3 |

\image(figures/tfrecord_io_sizes.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Compression has wrapper and block overhead; all modes retain the same three binary records.)
\alttext(Compression has wrapper and block overhead; all modes retain the same three binary records.)

> Checking the theory

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace d=dm::nn::data;
 const d::Example example{{"x",d::Feature::Floats({1,.5f})},{"label",d::Feature::Int64s({7})},{"id",d::Feature::Bytes({std::string("a\0b",3)})}};
 const std::vector<d::DenseSpec> schema{{"x",d::Feature::Kind::kFloat,2,std::nullopt},{"label",d::Feature::Kind::kInt64,1,std::nullopt},{"weight",d::Feature::Kind::kFloat,1,d::Feature::Floats({1})}};
 const auto parsed=d::ParseSingleExample(d::SerializeExample(example),schema);
 int bad=0;try{d::ParseSingleExample("",schema);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++bad;}
 const auto original=d::ReadBinary("build/tfrecord_plain");
 for(int mode=0;mode<3;++mode){auto bytes=original;if(mode==0)bytes[0]^=1;else if(mode==1)bytes[28]^=1;else bytes.pop_back();
 d::WriteBinary("build/tfrecord_bad",bytes);try{d::ReadTFRecords("build/tfrecord_bad");}catch(const std::runtime_error&){++bad;}}
 const std::string crc_input="123456789";const auto crc=d::Crc32c(reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t*>(crc_input.data()),crc_input.size());
 if(crc!=0xe3069283u||bad!=4||parsed[2].floats[0]!=1)return 1;
 std::print("CRC-32C check vector: 0x{:08x}.\n\nFloat values ({}, {}), label {}, default weight {}.\n\nMissing required feature plus three damaged streams rejected: {}.\n",crc,parsed[0].floats[0],parsed[0].floats[1],parsed[1].ints[0],parsed[2].floats[0],bad);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
CRC-32C check vector: 0xe3069283.

Float values (1, 0.5), label 7, default weight 1.

Missing required feature plus three damaged streams rejected: 4.
// result_end


> Conclusion

Record boundaries, binary payloads, compression and required/defaulted features remain distinct.
A checksum failure stops reading. The byte counts show that compression is a workload-dependent
choice; these tiny fixtures do not establish throughput or compression ratios for real training data.

> References

- [TensorFlow: TFRecord and tf.train.Example](https://www.tensorflow.org/tutorials/load_data/tfrecord).
- [Protocol Buffers encoding guide](https://protobuf.dev/programming-guides/encoding/).
